ProofSieve

The ProofSieve source and original documentation are licensed under Apache-2.0.

The EUDI mdoc examples derive from the EUDI Wallet OpenID4VP reference library.
The fixture and its projection retain the upstream Apache-2.0 terms.
See examples/signed/README.md and examples/signed/LICENSE-EUDI-OPENID4VP.txt.

The SD-JWT examples derived from RFC 9901 use the IETF Trust Revised BSD terms
for extracted code components. See examples/signed/LICENSE-RFC9901.txt.
Additional standards and example sources are listed in examples/credentials/README.md.

The optional Java acceptance bridge resolves European Commission Digital
Signature Services (DSS) separately under its LGPL-2.1 license. ProofSieve's
wheel and source archive contain no DSS binaries.
See https://github.com/esig/dss/blob/master/LICENSE.

The API Explorer includes the upstream Swagger UI distribution from SmartBear
Software under Apache-2.0. The original distribution's license, notice and
extracted third-party license comments accompany the vendored assets in
apps/api-docs/vendor/. The supplemental component inventory and license texts
are in apps/api-docs/vendor/THIRD-PARTY.LICENSE.txt.
